<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Basarab I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1351/1352</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Basarab I of Wallachia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Basarab I was the first independent ruler of Wallachia, first recorded in 1324, who united the Romanian lands between the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. In November 1330 his forces ambushed and defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary">Charles I of Hungary</a> at Posada, securing Wallachia's independence, and his descendants, the Basarab dynasty, ruled the principality for more than two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basarab-i.jpg" alt="Basarab I" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: not credited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basarab_I_of_Wallachia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
